Description:
 linuxmuster-base7 - linuxmuster.net configuration scripts
Changes:
 linuxmuster-base7 (1:7.4.24~edu) lmn74; urgency=low
 .
   * edulution fork. The package keeps its upstream name, so the epoch 1: is
     what makes it win against the same package from deb.linuxmuster.net.
   * The version carries the suffix ~edu on top of the epoch, so apt policy,
     dpkg -l and the motd show at a glance that this is the edulution build
     and not the upstream package. "~" sorts before the empty string, so
     1:7.4.24~edu stays below a hypothetical 1:7.4.24 while still outranking
     every upstream 7.x, which carries no epoch at all. The versioned
     dependencies on the fork's own packages therefore clamp on "(>=
     1:x.y.z~)", the Debian idiom that also accepts a tilde suffix.
   * Drop the hard dependency on linuxmuster-webui7 and depend on
     linuxmuster-api7 instead, which so far was only pulled in by the webui.
   * New setup step kz_ldap-config writes /etc/linuxmuster/tools/ldap.yml,
     the LDAP configuration linuxmuster-tools7 reads. Upstream those settings
     sat in /etc/linuxmuster/webui/config.yml, which only linuxmuster-webui7
     created. The schema belongs to tools7; this step only fills in the base
     DN, the server name and the global-binduser password that k_samba-users
     creates one step earlier.
   * z_final restarts linuxmuster-api instead of linuxmuster-webui.
   * The motd (etc/profile.d/Z99-linuxmuster.sh) makes the origin of the
     packages visible. Every version is printed with its ~edu suffix in
     edulution blue, so a half-migrated server stands out, and a framed note
     at the bottom names where the updates come from - or warns when ~edu
     packages are installed without the repository, because then nothing
     updates them any more. The epoch is dropped from the display: it is a
     packaging detail, and it would have turned the title into
     "LINUXMUSTER.NET 1:7". A server without a single edulution package shows
     neither the note nor a suffix and keeps the banner upstream has.
   * The "e" of edulution is set in italics, the way Euler's number is set in
     mathematics. Not with U+212F or U+2147, the codepoints meant for it:
     DejaVu Sans Mono, Liberation Mono and Ubuntu Mono carry neither, so most
     terminals would draw a replacement box and the fallback to a
     proportional font would shift the frame below.
   * The motd reads the versions with dpkg-query and prints "not installed"
     for what is missing. It queried linuxmuster-webui7, which this fork does
     not install, and edulution-linbo-gui7, which is not a dependency of this
     package either - both wrote a dpkg error across the banner on every
     login.
   * Pre-Depends on linuxmuster-common (>= 1:7.4.5~), so the fork cannot be
     mixed with the upstream package.
   * Release workflow publishes to edulution-io/edulution-package-server
     instead of linuxmuster/deb, into the Ubuntu codename resolute.
